From: Richard Fritz <gh@chaos4all.de>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu-bridge: Add Sony IMX241 (INT347F) to supported sensors

Note: ipu3-cio2 creates its media links and subdev nodes only once every
sensor in the fwnode graph has bound (cio2_notifier_complete()), so this
entry must only be added together with a working IMX241 driver; with
the imx241 driver (0006) both cameras work on the HP Pro x2 612 G2.

The Sony IMX241 is found with ACPI HID INT347F on IPU3 based devices
such as the HP Pro x2 612 G2, where it is the front camera on CSI-2
port 1 with 2 data lanes.

Add it to the list of sensors supported by ipu-bridge so that the
fwnode graph is built for it, with a link frequency of 498 MHz. The
TPS68470 clock on this machine is shared with the rear OV8858, which
runs it at 24 MHz, and the imx241 driver then uses pre-PLL divider 2
and multiplier 83: PLL 996 MHz, RAW10 on 2 lanes at 996 Mbit/s per
lane, link frequency 498 MHz. (The Windows driver uses a 19.2 MHz clock
and 499.2 MHz; the imx241 driver still supports that if it finds the
clock at 19.2 MHz, and warns that the link frequency is not listed.)

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Richard Fritz <gh@chaos4all.de>
---
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347A", 1, 360000000),
 	/* Omnivision OV7251 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347E", 1, 319200000),
+	/* Sony IMX241 */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347F", 1, 498000000),
 	/* Hynix Hi-556 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT3537", 1, 437000000),
 	/* Lontium lt6911uxe */
